+# ArbiLend — Security Audit Report
+
+**Scope**: `src/LendingMarket.sol`, `src/CollateralVault.sol`, `src/PriceOracle.sol`, `src/MarketProxy.sol`, `src/interfaces/*`
+**Commit**: `8883129` (working tree clean)
+**Target chain**: Arbitrum One
+**Compiler**: solc 0.8.28, optimizer on (200 runs)
+**Date**: 2026-08-27
+
+---
+
+## Verdict
+
+**Do not deploy this in two weeks.**
+
+Three functions that control the entire protocol — `upgradeTo`, `setOracle`,
+`setLiquidationThreshold` — have no access control at all. Any address can call
+them the moment the proxy is live and take everything. Separately, the health
+factor calculation divides before multiplying, which throws away all precision
+and silently converts your advertised 80% liquidation threshold into a hard 50%
+LTV cap, with every maximum-sized borrower sitting one wei of price movement
+away from a 5% penalty.
+
+These are not edge cases. C-1 through C-4 are reachable by anyone, on the first
+block, with no preconditions.
+
+I also verified the two Chainlink feed addresses in `README.md` against
+Chainlink's published Arbitrum reference-data directory. The USDC feed is
+correct. The wstETH feed is **stETH/USD** — it is not a wstETH feed, and pricing
+wstETH with it understates that collateral by the full wstETH exchange-rate
+premium (H-3).
+
+There is no test suite. Every finding below is from code reading; nothing has
+been executed. Get the fixes in, then get tests in, then re-audit.
+
+---
+
