+# Critical
+
+<a name="c-1"></a>
+## [C-1] `upgradeTo` has no access control — anyone takes over the entire protocol
+
+**Severity**: Critical
+**Category**: access-control, proxies
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:84-89`
+
+### Description
+
+```solidity
+function upgradeTo(address newImplementation) external {
+    assembly {
+        sstore(IMPLEMENTATION_SLOT, newImplementation)
+    }
+    emit Upgraded(newImplementation);
+}
+```
+
+No `onlyOwner`. No `initialized` check. Nothing. This is the canonical UUPS
+failure — an `_authorizeUpgrade` equivalent with an empty body — except here
+there is not even an empty modifier to give the reader pause.
+
+`MarketProxy` delegates every call to the implementation, so
+`MarketProxy.upgradeTo(x)` executes this body in the proxy's storage context and
+writes `x` into the proxy's ERC-1967 implementation slot.
+
+The blast radius is the whole system, not just the market. `CollateralVault.market`
+is immutable and set to the proxy address, and `CollateralVault.seize` is gated
+on `msg.sender == market`. Whoever controls the implementation controls
+`seize`, and therefore controls every deposit in the vault.
+
+### Proof of Concept
+
+1. Attacker deploys `Evil` with a function `drain(address token, address user, uint256 amt)` that calls `vault.seize(user, token, attacker, amt)`.
+2. Attacker calls `MarketProxy.upgradeTo(address(evil))`. It succeeds — there is no check.
+3. Attacker calls `MarketProxy.drain(wstETH, victim, victimBalance)` for every depositor.
+4. Attacker also sweeps the market's USDC balance (the treasury-seeded lending liquidity) with a second helper function.
+
+Total loss: all collateral in `CollateralVault` plus all USDC held by the market.
+Cost: one contract deployment and two transactions. No flash loan, no price
+move, no timing.
+
+### Recommendation
+
+Add the missing modifier, and validate the target:
+
+```solidity
+function upgradeTo(address newImplementation) external onlyOwner {
+    if (newImplementation.code.length == 0) revert NotAContract();
+    assembly {
+        sstore(IMPLEMENTATION_SLOT, newImplementation)
+    }
+    emit Upgraded(newImplementation);
+}
+```
+
+Beyond the immediate fix: put upgrades behind a timelock, and consider adopting
+OpenZeppelin's `UUPSUpgradeable`, which additionally enforces the
+`proxiableUUID` check that stops you from bricking the proxy by upgrading to a
+non-UUPS implementation.
+
