+<a name="m-4"></a>
+## [M-4] Listing a collateral token with no price feed bricks the entire market
+
+**Severity**: Medium
+**Category**: dos, oracles
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:107-114`
+
+**Description.** `listCollateral` pushes to `collateralTokens` and enables the
+token in the vault. It never checks that `oracle.feeds[token]` is set.
+
+`collateralValueUsd` iterates `collateralTokens` and calls `oracle.getPrice(token)`
+for every token where the user's balance is non-zero. `getPrice` reverts with
+`FeedNotSet` when the feed is missing.
+
+**Impact.** Between `listCollateral` and `setFeed` there is a window where any
+user who deposits the new token has an unpriceable position — `healthFactor`
+reverts, so their borrow, their withdrawal *and their liquidation* all revert.
+If a feed is later unset, or `setFeed` is called with the zero address, the same
+happens retroactively.
+
+`collateralTokens` has no removal path, so a token listed in error is permanent.
+
+**Recommendation.** Require the feed first, and add a getter to check it:
+
+```solidity
+function listCollateral(address token) external onlyOwner {
+    if (token == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();
+    if (address(oracle.feeds(token)) == address(0)) revert FeedNotSet(token);
+    ...
+}
+```
+
+Add a delisting path that stops new deposits while leaving withdrawal and
+liquidation open. Consider wrapping the `getPrice` call in `collateralValueUsd`
+in `try/catch` so one bad feed degrades one token rather than freezing every
+account (H-1 raises the same point for feed reverts generally).
+
