+<a name="m-5"></a>
+## [M-5] Vault accounting assumes exact, non-rebasing transfers
+
+**Severity**: Medium
+**Category**: erc20
+**Location**: `src/CollateralVault.sol:35-42`
+
+**Description.**
+
+```solidity
+IERC20(token).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+balanceOf[msg.sender][token] += amount;
+```
+
+The credited figure is the *requested* amount, not the amount received.
+
+- **Fee-on-transfer tokens**: the vault credits more than it holds. The last withdrawers find the vault short.
+- **Rebasing tokens**: `balanceOf` is a fixed snapshot that never tracks rebases. Positive rebases accrue to nobody and are stranded; a negative rebase (slashing) leaves the vault crediting more than it holds.
+
+wstETH is neither, so this is safe at launch. But the README says the DAO has
+asked for "a path to yield-bearing and rebasing collateral" — this code cannot
+take that path as written, and `listCollateral` has no way to detect the problem.
+
+**Recommendation.** Credit the measured delta:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 before = IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this));
+IERC20(token).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+uint256 received = IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this)) - before;
+balanceOf[msg.sender][token] += received;
+```
+
+That fixes fee-on-transfer. Rebasing needs a share-based accounting model
+(track shares, convert on read) rather than absolute balances — a design change,
+not a patch. Decide which you are supporting before the DAO's request turns into
+a listing, and document that rebasing tokens are unsupported until then.
+
