+<a name="m-9"></a>
+## [M-9] No minimum position size — dust positions become permanent bad debt
+
+**Severity**: Medium
+**Category**: defi-lending
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol:157-159, 197-207`
+
+**Description.** `borrow` accepts any amount including zero. There is no minimum
+debt and no minimum collateral.
+
+**Impact.** A position with $3 of debt costs more in gas to liquidate than the
+5% bonus returns, so nobody clears it. These accumulate as permanent bad debt
+(M-2), and each one is a `borrowers` entry that `liquidateAll` pays to iterate
+forever (H-7). On Arbitrum gas is cheap enough that creating thousands is
+affordable.
+
+The `amount == 0` case is the acute version and is covered in H-7; this is the
+broader economic point.
+
+**Recommendation.** Enforce a floor, denominated in USD so it survives price
+moves:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 public minDebtUsd; // e.g. 100e18
+
+// in _borrow, after updating principal:
+uint256 d = debtValueUsd(borrower);
+if (d != 0 && d < minDebtUsd) revert DebtTooSmall();
+```
+
+Also require that `repay` either clears the position entirely or leaves at least
+`minDebtUsd` outstanding, otherwise borrowers can partially repay down into dust.
+
