+<a name="m-10"></a>
+## [M-10] No pause or circuit breaker
+
+**Severity**: Medium
+**Category**: access-control
+**Location**: `src/LendingMarket.sol`, `src/CollateralVault.sol`
+
+**Description.** There is no way to halt the protocol. If a feed misbehaves, an
+exploit is discovered, or the sequencer misbehaves in a way not covered by H-2,
+the only lever is `upgradeTo` — which means writing, reviewing and deploying a
+new implementation under time pressure while the loss accrues.
+
+**Impact.** Incident response time is measured in however long it takes to ship
+a correct contract. For a market holding real collateral, that is the difference
+between a contained incident and a total one.
+
+**Recommendation.** Add a pause with asymmetric scope — this is the part teams
+usually get wrong. Pausing must stop `borrow` and `withdraw` but **must not**
+stop `repay` or `liquidate`: freezing repayment while interest accrues means
+borrowers are liquidated for a pause they could not act during, and freezing
+liquidation lets bad debt build silently.
+
+Give the pauser role to a low-latency multisig separate from the owner, and make
+unpausing require the full owner path.
+
